    "note": "Both floor votes were on Amended 2018-05-25. That amendment STRUCK the earlier \"California Do Not Sell List\" platform and crime for transferring a firearm to a listed person; what remains is a study and report by 1/1/2020, repealed 1/1/2024."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 29880 (Penal Code): (a) The Department of Justice shall study options for allowing a person to register himself or herself on a list or database that prohibits the person from being able to purchase a firearm. The department shall recommend an approach to allow a person to prohibit himself or herself from purchasing a firearm. (b) The department shall provide a report of its findings and recommendations to the Legislature no later than January 1, 2020.\nSection 29880 (Penal Code): Pursuant to Section 10231.5 of the Government Code, this section is repealed on January 1, 2024."
